% A large expression under many adornments.  Each adornment of p/6 reads
% its rule, and with it an expression of 1023 nodes, so the rewrite's
% limit, which counts a literal's size, one and one more per node, is
% outgrown in the search, after some fifty of the sixty-three patterns q/1
% calls p/6 with, each binding different columns; the rewrite is abandoned
% with a warning and the query answered from the whole program, with the
% same rows.  Counted in literals alone, the copies would stay far within
% the limit.  p/6 holds one tuple, so each call matches at most one and the
% whole program's join of the sixty-three calls stays one row wide.
b(1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1).
s(2).
s(1).

